  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7/1"/>To appease You with supplication,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7/2"/>Your servants have agreed,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7/3"/>be accessible to them
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7/4"/>and remember [Your assurances of] comfort;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7/5"/>do wonders for them in Your kindness,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7/6"/>and remove their [sins] stains,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7/7"/>Almighty! King,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7/8"/>Who sits on the throne of mercy,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_7/9"/>between Rosh Hashana and Yom Kippur.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
